WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.120
The hunt is on in "The Witcher" season 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.560
as fans of "The Witcher" video games will see&nbsp;
some very familiar faces riding in to run wild.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.640
Here's everything else that meant more than&nbsp;
you realized in "The Witcher" season 2.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.960
As fans may know well by now, Geralt is not&nbsp;
known for being particularly forthright.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.440
For this Witcher, less is always more.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.200
He takes Ciri to the Witcher stronghold, Kaer&nbsp;
Morhen, knowing that it will keep her safe. Upon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:33.120
their approach, Ciri notes its rundown appearance.&nbsp;
He offers a vague explanation, telling her,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.400
"There was an attack. A long&nbsp;
time ago, when I was a boy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.160
Almost wiped us all out. So now&nbsp;
we like to keep a low profile."

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.360
The sacking of Kaer Morhen is devastating for&nbsp;
Witchers, and it's detailed in the anime film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.200
The Witcher: Nightmare of the Wolf. The Netflix&nbsp;
film covers Vesemir's backstory. In his youth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.960
he dreams of escaping his misfortune, and he goes&nbsp;
on to become a Witcher and kill monsters for coin.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.080
In addition to this backstory, Nightmare of&nbsp;
the Wolf details the specifics of the downfall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.520
of Kaer Morhen. A powerful mage named Tetra&nbsp;
blames Witchers for the deaths of her family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.720
and comes up with a plot to destroy them.&nbsp;
This plan includes destroying mutagens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.320
which results in the loss of any means to create&nbsp;
more Witchers. This backstory gives more context&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.680
to Vesemir's grief over losing Ciri's blood&nbsp;
compound that would have made more of his kind.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.920
Part of Ciri's great loss is that she never&nbsp;
knew her parents. As we see in Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.360
The Law of Surprise ensures that, even&nbsp;
though Geralt initially balks at the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.680
Ciri's destiny is forever tied to&nbsp;
his, and he is responsible for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.400
Ciri's birth parents are removed from the&nbsp;
picture the moment Geralt helps her father, Duny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:51.040
secure Duny's union with Ciri's mother, Pavetta.&nbsp;
However, Ciri was first raised by her grandmother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.360
Queen Calanthe, who kept the details of&nbsp;
her lineage and fate a secret from her.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.720
Geralt reveals to her that he was at&nbsp;
her parents' wedding feast, causing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.320
Ciri to be intrigued because she has very little&nbsp;
knowledge about how her parents came to be wed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.800
Geralt never sugarcoats the truth, but&nbsp;
he does leave specific details out.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:16.640
"Your grandmother. She didn't want&nbsp;
your mother marrying a — an outsider."

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.000
True to form, Geralt is once again lighter&nbsp;
on the details, omitting the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.320
Ciri's mother fell in love with her father&nbsp;
while he was cursed to look like a hedgehog.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.440
Geralt does this as a kindness, not wanting&nbsp;
to sully Ciri's perception of her grandmother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.560
But he is careful for another key reason. He&nbsp;
knows exactly what it means to be an outsider.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.040
Going through life, he experiences judgment&nbsp;
from the world at large for being a Witcher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.800
He knows the pain that brings and what&nbsp;
it is like to remain on the outside.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.520
Being a parent is a core theme of&nbsp;
The Witcher Season 2. Until now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.640
Geralt spent most of his life alone, only&nbsp;
having to care for himself and his horse, Roach.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.840
Parenthood — albeit surrogate fatherhood — is new&nbsp;
to him, and he doesn't always do the right thing.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.680
When Geralt and Ciri travel to Kaer Morhen,&nbsp;
Vesemir advises him on the truths of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:11.040
a parent. Geralt often expects Ciri to do as&nbsp;
she's told and quickly realizes that raising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.160
a child is not as easy as bending a child to&nbsp;
one's will. He learns this especially after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:22.720
the death of his brother-in-arms, Eskel. Eskel is&nbsp;
infected by a Leshen and turned into a monster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.120
After Geralt is forced to kill him,&nbsp;
Vesemir laments the loss, telling Geralt,

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.640
"If it were your child, you'd be&nbsp;
going crazy to figure it out."

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:36.240
"What you missed. What you&nbsp;
could have done differently."

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.680
The Witchers at Kaer Morhen are like&nbsp;
sons to him, and his grief is powerful.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.400
At the time, Geralt feels like he can&nbsp;
sympathize with Vesemir's emotions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.080
He is a father of sorts now and would&nbsp;
do anything for Ciri. But he doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.680
fully understand the overwhelming&nbsp;
weight of parenthood until later.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.680
After bringing Ciri to a temple so she can learn&nbsp;
to control her chaos, he reunites with Yennefer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:05.200
Though the reunion is romantic at first, Geralt&nbsp;
quickly learns his mistake in trusting her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.640
Yennefer steals Ciri in a bid to reinstate her&nbsp;
power. Geralt is not especially surprised at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.920
Yennefer's actions but feels the heartache of&nbsp;
losing someone who is effectively his child.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.200
Stregobor is easily one of the most&nbsp;
detestable antagonists in "The Witcher."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:27.440
He operates with no morals, asking Istredd to spy&nbsp;
on Yennefer due to her elven blood in Season 1.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.400
He makes no show of hiding his prejudices and&nbsp;
outwardly hurts people for his own enjoyment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.880
This includes his treatment of Yennefer&nbsp;
in Season 2. Because she is a quarter elf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.640
Nilfgaard's alignment with the elves&nbsp;
calls her loyalty into question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.560
Fueled by suspicions that she is&nbsp;
a spy, Stregobor tortures her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:50.080
trying to enter her mind for secrets. He defends&nbsp;
his actions by stating that all he ever cared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.200
about was protecting their society, and he&nbsp;
tells a group of mages as much in episode 3.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.560
"I've always tried to protect our&nbsp;
institutions. To protect you."
 &nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.080
But this is a weak defense. Stregobor&nbsp;
has often exhibited hatred of women.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.080
He refers to Yennefer as being&nbsp;
lesser because of her blood.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.960
"The only Cintra hates more than mages is elves."

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.000
This attitude is a mirror from Season 1 and his&nbsp;
treatment of Renfri. Renfri was among 60 girls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.760
born during a lunar eclipse. Because of this,&nbsp;
Stregobor decreed that they should all be killed.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:32.560
"Renfri kills for pleasure. She is a&nbsp;
monster. She is the last of Lilith's women."

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.320
Renfri suffered at the hands of Stregobor, and&nbsp;
his abuses continued into the present timeline.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:45.200
"Stregobor's man raped me,&nbsp;
robbed me and let me go."
 &nbsp;

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.160
He uses the excuse that he is doing it for&nbsp;
his people when he is really just prejudiced.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.840
Many plot points have been teased and built up&nbsp;
since the first episode of The Witcher series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.720
However, an element that fans of the show may&nbsp;
not be familiar with materializes in the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.640
episode. After Ciri, Geralt, and Yennefer&nbsp;
dispel Voleth Meir in a parallel sphere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.080
the newfound family sees something they did not&nbsp;
expect: A horde of ghostly riders charging them.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:19.360
"Child of the elder blood, starry eyed&nbsp;
daughter of chaos, join our hunt!"

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.160
After they portal back to safety, Ciri&nbsp;
knows they aren't completely safe yet.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.120
"Were those the Wraiths of Mörhogg?"
 &nbsp;

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:33.040
Geralt confirms her suspicions, merely saying&nbsp;
those riders are The Wild Hunt, also known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.480
The Wraiths of Mörhogg. The Wild Hunt will be&nbsp;
integral to The Witcher world going forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.520
The ghost riders are set up in Andrzej Sapkowski's&nbsp;
books and are heavily featured in The Witcher 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:49.920
video game. These riders are intent on capturing&nbsp;
slaves, and they mark Ciri as their next target.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:55.200
Her Elder blood draws them to her and makes&nbsp;
her desirable because of how powerful she is.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.080
The introduction of The Wild&nbsp;
Hunt is only the start of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.080
plotline involving this terrifying&nbsp;
antagonist from The Witcher canon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.360
Ciri and her new family will have&nbsp;
to look out for it in Season 3.

